Subject: [PATCH 27/38] =?UTF-8?q?perf(agents):=20trim=20per-cycle=20contex?=
 =?UTF-8?q?t=20intake=20=E2=80=94=20mail=20cursor=20+=20mid-weight=20patro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?l=20prime=20+=20nudge=20de-dup?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gfork-47p.4 (P1): reduce per-loop context accretion for persistent agents (headroom on top of .2's recycle). Three levers: (B) mail_check.go inject-once cursor — acked-unread normal/low mail collapses to a counter line instead of re-injecting full every prompt boundary, urgent/high always re-inject until read, legacy mailboxes (empty DeliveryState) unchanged (zero regression). (A) handoff.go/prime.go/prime_output.go — a patrol-cycle handoff marker triggers a mid-weight lite prime for deacon/witness (~5-line identity + 'gt prime'/'gt formula show' pointers instead of the ~17KB role template), keeping directives/CONTEXT.md/memory/patrol-status + truncated checklist; refinery is carved out (keeps the full formula — its truncation is the deferred gfork-47p.4.1); witness parked/docked and deacon paused correctness gates preserved verbatim. (C) nudge/queue.go — de-dup identical (Sender,Message,Kind) nudges on drain with an (xN) suffix.

Validated this session: gofumpt/vet/build green; internal/cmd + internal/nudge test-race green (Lever-B escalation carve-out + refinery carve-out both covered by tests; prime_molecule.go byte-untouched). E2E soak pending (lead gate: gt prime|wc -c deacon full-vs-lite byte-check + live deacon cycle).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
